      text="""{
    "Introduction to Python for Data Science": "Python is widely adopted in data science due to its scalability, readability, and rich community support. Data science integrates programming skills with mathematical and statistical concepts to collect, interpret, and make decisions based on data observations. The foundational curriculum introduces Python programming concepts as the primary tool for data science workflows.",
    "Data Manipulation with Pandas": "Data manipulation involves utilizing specialized libraries such as NumPy and Pandas to structure, analyze, and process numerical and categorical datasets. Operations include array handling, statistical calculations (such as t-tests using scipy.stats and numpy), and efficient data indexing and transformation.",
    "Data Cleaning and Preparation": "Data cleaning and preparation covers working with various file formats, text encodings (ASCII and Unicode), and input/output handling. Concepts include understanding sequential versus random access in files, processing line-by-line data with newline characters, and managing persistent storage on disk to retain input datasets across program runs.",
    "Exploratory Data Analysis and Visualization": "Exploratory data analysis involves inspecting, summarizing, and visually representing data characteristics to uncover underlying patterns, distributions, and relationships. Core libraries typically include Matplotlib and Seaborn to generate plots and graphs that assist in interpreting data prior to modeling.",
    "Introduction to Machine Learning Models": "Introduction to machine learning covers fundamental paradigms such as unsupervised learning, clustering approaches, and grouping data based on similarities and distance metrics without prior output labels. It establishes basic statistical knowledge and predictive concepts required for data science applications."
}"""
